lisa-design:
Regal unassigned-return-value fix in eks_nodegroup_require_scaling_headroom.rego: `object.get(current, "desired_at_or_above_min", false) != false` instead of `== true`. A bare expression in Rego succeeds for any defined value except `false`, so `!= false` keeps the exact semantics (null, "no", 0 still count as at-or-above-min); `== true` would change behaviour and is left as an open question. data.json keys get line-scoped `# regal ignore:unresolved-reference` trailing comments (no repo .regal config, so CI keeps the shared one). Fix errors only: the 13 Regal warnings are left as they are.
